      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_17",
        on: "start",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("Humans, halt! Who dares bring an army into the dwarvish hills?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Haldric II",
            text: _("We come to make a bargain with you."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("Well, state your business and be done with it. And if we don’t like what you say, you leave!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Haldric II",
            text: _("Have you heard of the Ruby of Fire?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("Yes... your first king brought it from over the sea, right? You own it."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Haldric II",
            text: _("Correct. However, we have a problem with it."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("What sort of problem?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Haldric II",
            text: _("Some form of magical aura makes those around the stone act... strangely. I noticed it with my father. The longer he stayed near the stone, the more arrogant, almost evil, he became."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("So, what do you want me to do? I don’t see how this relates to us dwarves."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Haldric II",
            text: _("When the elves came to Tath, about five years ago, they spoke of a mage named Crelanu, and of his advice about the ruby. He said that the radiance of the stone could be contained, and that doing so would stop the stone’s effect."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("And what... you want us to do this, contain the radiance of the stone? By making an artifact of some kind?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Haldric II",
            text: _("Exactly. I want you to craft it into a mighty artifact that will not only leverage the stone’s power, but contain it also."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("Well... I think we can make a deal, but I’m not sure. I’ll have to ask the clan leaders."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Haldric II",
            text: _("If you are not authorized to make a deal, send out someone who is, and I will bargain with him."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("They would refuse to come. You must come into the caves and go to the city in person, or send a representative."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Haldric II",
            text: _("I can always take my offer to another clan more friendly to its potential patrons. You are not the only smiths in the Northlands!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("Uh, no, wait! Let’s talk business — how much will you pay us to do this for you?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Haldric II",
            text: _("Five thousand pieces of silver."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("You said you wanted a powerful magical artifact, not a child’s playtoy! So... twenty thousand, minimum. The crafting of this will take us many years, you must pay us well."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Haldric II",
            text: _("Ten thousand."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("Nothing below fifteen!"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Haldric II",
            text: _("Then no deal. I’ll gather my things and go to another dwarvish clan now."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("Fine then — ten thousand... now, what exactly do you want us to make the stone into?"),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Haldric II",
            text: _("I want you to make it into a sceptre. A gold and ruby sceptre to all appearances. We shall call it the Sceptre of Fire."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Rugnur",
            text: _("I’ll see what I can do. But I will need five thousand silver in advance to pay for the materials."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Haldric II",
            text: _("Very well. I have the silver here, ready to ship, and I will send someone over with the stone itself. He will stay with you as you make the sceptre, and make sure you get it done on time. I expect it done before my reign as king is ended."),
          },
          {
            tag: "spawn",
            id: "u_3",
            type: "Caravan",
            side: 1,
            x: 9,
            y: 28,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:spawn_unit",
            unit: "u_3",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:make_loyal",
            unit: "u_3",
          },
          {
            tag: "spawn",
            id: "u_4",
            type: "Caravan",
            side: 1,
            x: 10,
            y: 28,
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
